Step 19 — Healthcare Traffic Criticality Classification

This is where we introduce the healthcare-specific part without AI.

No ML. No prediction model. No dataset training.

We will use a deterministic rule-based SDN traffic classification system.

Also, this is not yet a live-data step, so there is nothing to decide about smartwatch integration yet. When we reach the first step where live data could be added, I'll ask you before doing anything.

What Step 19 does

Not every healthcare packet should have the same network priority.

For example, we'll define three application traffic classes:

CRITICAL
URGENT
NORMAL

The classifier will assign a class from supplied physiological/test values using configurable prototype thresholds.

Then Step 20 will use the class to change the QoS cost weights.

Conceptually:

Health/application data
        ↓
Rule-based classifier
        ↓
CRITICAL / URGENT / NORMAL
        ↓
SDN QoS policy
        ↓
Cost weights
        ↓
Routing decision

For this prototype we'll use heart rate and SpO₂ as example inputs. These thresholds are demonstration rules for the networking prototype, not clinical decision rules.

